Build SUCCESS. Classes are in .\out

How to run (set MODPKICA_BASE to your PKI root first):
  set MODPKICA_BASE=C:\path\to\your\pki_root

  [1] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.MAIN
      (GUI auto starts at http://localhost:8080)
  [2] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.WebAdmin
      (GUI only)
  [3] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.Admin
  [4] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.MakeRoot "CN=Root,O=Org,C=CN" 2048 sha256 RSA
  [5] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.MakeCert "CN=www.test.com" 2048 sha256 1 1 0 1 "www.test.com" null null ROOTSERIAL RSA
      (ROOTSERIAL = CERTS.txt 中 R 类型根证书的序列号，多根模型已废除 root 别名)
  [6] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.RootGetCrl
  [7] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.CertVerify cert.crt
  [8] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;BC185\*;lib\*" modpkica.Auto revoke 1234567890 1
  [9] java "-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8" -cp "out;debug_test\classes;BC185\*;lib\*" ModpkicaUnitTest
      (unit tests: compile + run, requires the [1/2] build above)

          (If compilation fails, the command is NOT executed.)

Note: PKI folder layout (CERTS.txt, ROOT, CA, CERT, KEY, OCSP,
      TIMSTAMP, WebPublic, CONFIG.txt, logs.log) is created at MODPKICA_BASE.
